          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: शृणोति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शृणोति (śṛṇoti) — \"he, she or it hears\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From √श्रु (śru), 'to hear' — the same root as Latin clueo and Greek kleos, 'fame', which is what gets heard about you. It gives श्रुति (śruti), 'that which is heard': the Vedas, as against smṛti, 'that which is remembered'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more everyday action. Three follow, and each reuses the ones before."
            }
          ]
        },
